1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,300
Brazilian agencies require
a guarantee on every lease.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,550
When tenants don't pay,

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:09,950
agencies cover it themselves.
Other solutions take up to 60 days.

4
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:12,600
MUTAV backs the agency, on Solana.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
19 agencies signed letters of intent.
For the hackathon, we built the protocol.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,400
Is every guarantee really backed? First,
let's register Ana's guarantee: R$18,000.

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:28,900
On-chain, she's just an ID,
no personal data.

8
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:33,700
The reserve holds BRS, a Brazilian
stablecoin from Nora Finance,

9
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:37,000
and anyone can check

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,700
it meets the coverage
the reserve admin sets.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,800
Let's try one more lease.
That needs R$45,000; we have R$44,500.

12
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:48,400
Refused.

13
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,000
We can't promise
what we can't back.

14
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:59,000
What happens when Ana pays late?

15
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,450
The agency files a claim,
our operator verifies it,

16
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:08,450
the reserve pays out,
within the multisig's limits,

17
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:14,700
and our PIX to the agency
is recorded on-chain.

18
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,400
Filed to settled, on-chain:
65 seconds.

19
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,200
Not 60 days.

20
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:28,200
And it's all public: every guarantee,
claim and account,

21
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:31,600
live at reserve.mutav.finance.

22
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,800
Today, our team signs each step
from our operator console.

23
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:41,200
Next, a server wallet
in our platform signs them,

24
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:44,600
within limits
the program enforces.

25
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:49,100
How does the reserve grow? Six months
of our pilot plan, simulated locally,

26
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:53,100
growing it
to R$1 million.

27
00:01:55,100 --> 00:02:00,100
New capital, guarantee fees and yield come in.
Small claims go out.

28
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:05,600
So the reserve can back more leases.

29
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:12,800
MUTAV: a reserve you can see,

30
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:15,800
payments that run themselves,
and capital that works.

31
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:17,970
Brazil's on-chain rent guarantee.
